        "reply_text": "You can approach the Rent Authority to file an application or appeal accompanied by affidavits and documents. If the landlord fails to make a refund where they exercised the right of recovery under specific sections, they may be liable to pay simple interest.\n\nKeep your tenancy agreement and receipt ready as proof of your security deposit.\n\nWhat I understood: You moved out of your rental property in Lucknow in October 2026, and your landlord has withheld your security deposit of Rs 16,000 even though you have your agreement and receipt.\n\nThe security deposit shall be refunded to the tenant on the date of taking over vacant possession of the premises from the tenant, after making due deduction of any liability of the tenant, provided the security deposit for residential premises does not exceed two months' rent.\n\nI cannot guarantee any outcome or promise that you will win; the final result depends on the facts and the authority's decision.\n\nWhat is the specific reason given by the landlord for withholding your security deposit?\n\nSource: Uttar Pradesh Regulation of Urban Premises Tenancy Act, 2021, section 33\nSource: Uttar Pradesh Regulation of Urban Premises Tenancy Act, 2021, section 24\nSource: Uttar Pradesh Regulation of Urban Premises Tenancy Act, 2021, section 11\n\nWhat I could not verify:\n- landlord contact details\n\nThis is legal information, not legal advice.",
